{"method":"item/started","params":{"item":{"type":"mcpToolCall","id":"exec-0f70e3b6-6852-4a31-8e79-fe5989497cd5","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github.search_issues","status":"inProgress","arguments":{"query":"repo:rickylabs/netscript is:issue 1881","repository_full_name":"rickylabs/netscript","topn":5},"appContext":{"connectorId":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","linkId":"link_69b013b6269c819190bfa7300fc08da0","resourceUri":null,"appName":"GitHub","actionName":"search_issues"},"pluginId":null,"readOnlyHint":true,"result":null,"error":null,"durationMs":null},"threadId":"01a06491-c069-7610-999b-e4f3efa4096f","turnId":"01a06491-c0b5-7811-a584-1b84e145973e","startedAtMs":1788393869627},"emittedAtMs":1788393869627}
{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"mcpToolCall","id":"exec-0f70e3b6-6852-4a31-8e79-fe5989497cd5","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github.search_issues","status":"completed","arguments":{"query":"repo:rickylabs/netscript is:issue 1881","repository_full_name":"rickylabs/netscript","topn":5},"appContext":{"connectorId":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","linkId":"link_69b013b6269c819190bfa7300fc08da0","resourceUri":null,"appName":"GitHub","actionName":"search_issues"},"pluginId":null,"readOnlyHint":true,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Action completed."}],"structuredContent":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1881","title":"test(aspire): clean-machine quickstart canary runs the root README sequence without manual recovery (#863 gate 3)","issue_number":1881,"body":"> Part of #863 (gate 3 of 3). Split out by the Aspire 13.5 topic supervisor so that #863's remainder is\n> not stranded when S8 (#1720 / PR #1754) closes **gate 1 only**. Sibling lane: #1880 (gate 2).\n\n## Scope — #863's gate 3, verbatim\n\n> the clean-machine quickstart sequence (as printed in the root README) runs end-to-end without manual\n> recovery.\n\n## Why this needs its own lane\n\n#863 carries three `gate:` boxes and **S8 owns gate 1 only** (the bounded, actionable `db init`\ntimeout). PR #1754 therefore carries `Part of #863` rather than a closing keyword. Gates 2 and 3 had\n**no owner** — a search of open issues referencing #863 returned only #1720 and the epic #1712 — so\nwithout explicit lanes #863 would either sit open behind two unassigned boxes or be closed on gate 1's\nevidence alone.\n\n## What gate 3 actually asks\n\nThis is a **clean-machine canary**, and the two words carry the whole requirement:\n\n- **clean machine** — no warm Docker images, no pre-existing volumes or networks, no prior\n  `.netscript/` state, no cached Aspire artifacts. A pass on a machine that has already run the suite\n  proves very little; the failures this gate exists to catch are first-run failures.\n- **as printed in the root README** — the commands executed must be the ones a new user actually reads,\n  copied verbatim. If the README's sequence needs a step that isn't printed, that is the finding, and\n  the fix is the README, not the transcript.\n- **without manual recovery** — no retries, no \"run it again and it works\", no undocumented cleanup\n  between steps. Any manual intervention is a failure of this gate even if the end state is correct.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] The exact command sequence printed in the root README is executed on a genuinely clean\n      environment, and the transcript is attached.\n- [ ] The run completes **without manual recovery** — any retry, out-of-band cleanup, or undocumented\n      step is recorded as a failure and drives a README or product fix rather than being worked around\n      in the transcript.\n- [ ] Divergence between the README's printed sequence and what actually has to be run is reported as a\n      defect against the README.\n- [ ] Cleanup afterwards proves the four-part zero baseline and **leaves any foreign or unknown-owner\n      resource unchanged** — see #1855, where an exact-AppHost cleanup removed a foreign network while\n      the suite's own gate reported PASS.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Does **not** cover #863's gate 1 (S8 / #1720 / PR #1754) or gate 2 (#1880, health-probe false\n  negative).\n- Requires the **globally serialized runtime lease** and a clean baseline; do not take one unprompted.\n- Depends on gate 2 (#1880) only insofar as an uncorrected `Running`/`Unhealthy` false negative may\n  itself force manual recovery during the quickstart — if that happens, it is evidence for #1880, not a\n  reason to relax this gate.\n\n## Notes\n\nMilestone matches the parent (#863, `0.0.7`); the coordinator should retarget if this slips past the\ncanary. This is a natural **canary-admission** gate rather than a per-PR CI gate.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1881","display_title":"test(aspire): clean-machine quickstart canary runs the root README sequence without manual recovery (#863 gate 3)"},{"url":"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/863","title":"scaffold: `netscript db init` can block indefinitely on an Unhealthy-but-Running Postgres resource (clean-machine quickstart flake)","issue_number":863,"body":"Found by the #816 adversarial pass (Sol·xhigh, 2026-07-18) running the printed quickstart on a clean machine with a cold `DENO_DIR`:\n\n- fresh scaffold (`--db postgres --service`), `aspire restore` + `aspire start` both exit 0;\n- Aspire reports the Postgres resource as **`Running` but `Unhealthy`** — health probe throws `NpgsqlException: Exception while reading from stream` (read timeout) while the Postgres container log says it is ready;\n- `netscript db init --name init` stays `Waiting` on that resource **beyond five minutes** with no progress, no timeout, and no actionable message; it had to be interrupted.\n\nIsolation: after interrupting, `db generate` (21s) and `db seed` (11s) succeed, and after a second `aspire start` the app's `/health` returns healthy — so the generated app is fine; the failure is the health-probe/readiness interaction plus `db init`'s unbounded wait.\n\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] gate: `db init` bounds its wait on dependency readiness with a clear, actionable timeout message (naming the unhealthy resource and the probe error);\n- [ ] gate: the Postgres health-probe false-negative (`Running`/`Unhealthy` with ready container log) is reproduced and fixed or explained with a documented readiness step the scaffold prints;\n- [ ] gate: the clean-machine quickstart sequence (as printed in the root README) runs end-to-end without manual recovery.\n\nEvidence: `.llm/runs/beta11-cli--orchestrator/slices/g14-816-main-readme/adversarial.md` (branch `docs/816-main-readme`), Gate log rows for the quickstart run.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/863","display_title":"scaffold: `netscript db init` can block indefinitely on an Unhealthy-but-Running Postgres resource (clean-machine quickstart flake)"}]},"_meta":null},"error":null,"durationMs":501},"threadId":"01a06491-c069-7610-999b-e4f3efa4096f","turnId":"01a06491-c0b5-7811-a584-1b84e145973e","completedAtMs":1788393870129},"emittedAtMs":1788393870131}
