{"method":"item/started","params":{"item":{"type":"mcpToolCall","id":"exec-78cdfa4a-beb7-443a-9668-b386596b9a1d","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github.create_pull_request","status":"inProgress","arguments":{"repository_full_name":"rickylabs/netscript","title":"test(e2e): walk the root README quickstart verbatim on the clean prod runner (#863 gate 3)","body":"## Summary\n\nAdds a clean-runner E2E suite that parses and executes the root README Quickstart in printed order against an exact published JSR CLI. The suite permits only the documented version and service-port substitutions, records every command as its own no-retry gate, and retains the existing ownership-proving cleanup tail.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Archetype / area: CLI/tooling E2E gate + root Quickstart documentation\n- Closes #1881\n- Part of #863\n- Parent epic: #1712\n\n## Slices\n\n- [x] S0 Lock current research, design, and gate plan — `75c41ee15`\n- [ ] S1 Add README markers, executable readiness, pure parser, and drift tests\n- [ ] S2 Register and prove the no-retry `readme.quickstart` suite\n- [ ] S3 Wire the hosted production runner (isolated workflow commit)\n\n## Validation\n\n- Scoped check — PASS (223 files, no diagnostics)\n- CLI E2E tests — PASS (302 passed, 0 failed)\n- Scoped format — PASS (223 files, no findings)\n- Scoped lint — baseline tooling refusal: zero findings; seven unchanged standalone desktop fixture files cannot resolve their existing root `catalog:` dependency\n- Runtime suites — NOT RUN locally; no runtime lease, hosted next-canary proof only\n\n## Harness\n\n- Run dir: `.llm/runs/research-aspire-13.5-adoption--0.0.7/slices/leaf-1881/`\n- Phase: impl — see per-slice comments and committed artifacts.\n- PLAN-EVAL: N/A; the coordinator supplied the exact baseline, contract, substitutions, gates, runtime boundary, and commit ordering.\n- Do not merge until the mandatory separate-session IMPL-EVAL and hosted canary evidence are complete.\n\n## Drift / Debt\n\n- Minor: the parent research artifact named in the brief is absent at the pinned baseline; Aspire 13.5.3 wait syntax was re-verified directly.\n- Significant baseline tooling drift: the exact lint wrapper refuses the pre-existing standalone desktop fixture configuration; no lint findings are reported.\n- No new or deepened architecture debt.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Root README marker block and executable readiness command are parser- and drift-tested.\n- [ ] `readme.quickstart` exposes one no-retry receipt gate per printed command and preserves foreign-resource cleanup doctrine.\n- [ ] Hosted `readme.quickstart` transcript at a canary tag is attached.\n- [ ] Separate-session IMPL-EVAL PASS is recorded.","head":"test/aspire-1881-readme-quickstart","base":"main","draft":true,"maintainer_can_modify":true},"appContext":{"connectorId":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","linkId":"link_69b013b6269c819190bfa7300fc08da0","resourceUri":null,"appName":"GitHub","actionName":"create_pull_request"},"pluginId":null,"readOnlyHint":false,"result":null,"error":null,"durationMs":null},"threadId":"01a06491-c069-7610-999b-e4f3efa4096f","turnId":"01a06491-c0b5-7811-a584-1b84e145973e","startedAtMs":1788394085058},"emittedAtMs":1788394085058}
