{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"mcpToolCall","id":"exec-ed3f4aa9-31c0-4346-a521-59f2afb15121","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github.fetch_issue_comments","status":"completed","arguments":{"issue_number":1881,"repo_full_name":"rickylabs/netscript"},"appContext":{"connectorId":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","linkId":"link_69b013b6269c819190bfa7300fc08da0","resourceUri":null,"appName":"GitHub","actionName":"fetch_issue_comments"},"pluginId":null,"readOnlyHint":true,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Action completed."}],"structuredContent":{"comments":[{"url":"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1881#issuecomment-5517708920","body":"## Triage (Aspire 13.5 topic supervisor, main `ba6f1f49a`)\n\n**Substrate exists, target is wrong.** The production canary already runs a clean-runner walk of a documented sequence from the exact published JSR CLI (`e2e-cli-prod.yml` → `deno task e2e:cli run quickstart.walk --source jsr --cli jsr:@netscript/cli@<version> --cleanup`). GitHub-hosted runners satisfy \"clean machine\" by construction (no warm images, volumes, `.netscript/`, or Aspire cache). But `quickstart.walk` mirrors **`docs/site/quickstart.vto`** (`QUICKSTART_DOCUMENTED_COMMANDS`, pinned by `tests/presentation/quickstart-command-drift_test.ts`), not the **root README**. Nothing pins the README's printed sequence, and it already diverges:\n\n| Root README (printed) | `quickstart.walk` (executed) | Gate-3 reading |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `netscript init my-app --db postgres --service --yes` | `netscript init my-app --db postgres --yes` + `netscript service add --name users --with-client` | README path (`--service`) is never walked on a clean runner |\n| `netscript db init --name init` / `db generate` / `db seed` (no `--db`) | `… --db postgres` on all three | README relies on the scaffold default; unverified |\n| `curl http://localhost:<port>/health` | `deno task check` | README's payoff step is never executed |\n| prose: \"wait until the `postgres` resource reports healthy\" | no equivalent step | an undocumented **manual readiness wait** sits between step 3 and 4 — exactly the #1880 / gate-2 seam |\n| — | `aspire restore` with `maxRetries: 2` | a retry is \"manual recovery\" under this gate's own definition; the README-verbatim walk must run it once |\n\n**Proposed slice (gate code only, `packages/cli/e2e/**`; WSL Codex lane; no product code):**\n\n1. `readme.quickstart` suite: parse the root README's `bash` fences between new `<!-- readme-quickstart:start/end -->` markers, strip comments, substitute only `<version>` (published version) and `<port>` (from the scaffold console output / receipt), and execute **verbatim, in order, no retries**. Any divergence from what has to be run is reported as a README defect (acceptance box 3), not patched in the transcript.\n2. Drift test pinning the README block the same way `quickstart-command-drift_test.ts` pins `quickstart.vto`.\n3. The \"wait until postgres reports healthy\" prose becomes an executable line in the README (e.g. `aspire wait postgres --status healthy --apphost aspire`) or the walk records it as a defect — either way the manual step disappears.\n4. `e2e-cli-prod.yml` runs `readme.quickstart` after `quickstart.walk`; the four-part zero-baseline cleanup and foreign-resource non-mutation are inherited from `createCleanupGates()` (post-#1855 ownership proof).\n5. Evidence for closure: one `e2e-cli-prod` run at a canary tag with the `readme.quickstart` transcript attached; that run is the canary-admission gate.\n\nDependency: none hard on #1880 — if the README walk fails at the readiness seam, that is gate-2 evidence, per this issue's Boundaries.\n\nNot started: requires a canary-admission slot; runtime is exercised only on the hosted prod runner (no local lease needed). Recommend `status:plan`, milestone stays `0.0.7` unless the coordinator retargets after Canary 7.\n","user":{"login":"rickylabs","name":"rickylabs","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129366361?v=4","id":129366361},"id":5517708920,"pull_request_review_id":null,"in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"review":null,"side":null,"line":null,"start_line":null,"path":null,"body_html":"<h2 dir=\"auto\">Triage (Aspire 13.5 topic supervisor, main <code class=\"notranslate\">ba6f1f49a</code>)</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Substrate exists, target is wrong.</strong> The production canary already runs a clean-runner walk of a documented sequence from the exact published JSR CLI (<code class=\"notranslate\">e2e-cli-prod.yml</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">deno task e2e:cli run quickstart.walk --source jsr --cli jsr:@netscript/cli@&lt;version&gt; --cleanup</code>). GitHub-hosted runners satisfy \"clean machine\" by construction (no warm images, volumes, <code class=\"notranslate\">.netscript/</code>, or Aspire cache). But <code class=\"notranslate\">quickstart.walk</code> mirrors <strong><code class=\"notranslate\">docs/site/quickstart.vto</code></strong> (<code class=\"notranslate\">QUICKSTART_DOCUMENTED_COMMANDS</code>, pinned by <code class=\"notranslate\">tests/presentation/quickstart-command-drift_test.ts</code>), not the <strong>root README</strong>. Nothing pins the README's printed sequence, and it already diverges:</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\"table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Root README (printed)</th>\n<th><code class=\"notranslate\">quickstart.walk</code> (executed)</th>\n<th>Gate-3 reading</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">netscript init my-app --db postgres --service --yes</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">netscript init my-app --db postgres --yes</code> + <code class=\"notranslate\">netscript service add --name users --with-client</code></td>\n<td>README path (<code class=\"notranslate\">--service</code>) is never walked on a clean runner</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">netscript db init --name init</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">db generate</code> / <code class=\"notranslate\">db seed</code> (no <code class=\"notranslate\">--db</code>)</td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">… --db postgres</code> on all three</td>\n<td>README relies on the scaffold default; unverified</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">curl http://localhost:&lt;port&gt;/health</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">deno task check</code></td>\n<td>README's payoff step is never executed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>prose: \"wait until the <code class=\"notranslate\">postgres</code> resource reports healthy\"</td>\n<td>no equivalent step</td>\n<td>an undocumented <strong>manual readiness wait</strong> sits between step 3 and 4 — exactly the <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5314539607\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1880\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1880/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1880\">#1880</a> / gate-2 seam</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>—</td>\n<td><code class=\"notranslate\">aspire restore</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">maxRetries: 2</code></td>\n<td>a retry is \"manual recovery\" under this gate's own definition; the README-verbatim walk must run it once</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Proposed slice (gate code only, <code class=\"notranslate\">packages/cli/e2e/**</code>; WSL Codex lane; no product code):</strong></p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">readme.quickstart</code> suite: parse the root README's <code class=\"notranslate\">bash</code> fences between new <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;!-- readme-quickstart:start/end --&gt;</code> markers, strip comments, substitute only <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;version&gt;</code> (published version) and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;port&gt;</code> (from the scaffold console output / receipt), and execute <strong>verbatim, in order, no retries</strong>. Any divergence from what has to be run is reported as a README defect (acceptance box 3), not patched in the transcript.</li>\n<li>Drift test pinning the README block the same way <code class=\"notranslate\">quickstart-command-drift_test.ts</code> pins <code class=\"notranslate\">quickstart.vto</code>.</li>\n<li>The \"wait until postgres reports healthy\" prose becomes an executable line in the README (e.g. <code class=\"notranslate\">aspire wait postgres --status healthy --apphost aspire</code>) or the walk records it as a defect — either way the manual step disappears.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">e2e-cli-prod.yml</code> runs <code class=\"notranslate\">readme.quickstart</code> after <code class=\"notranslate\">quickstart.walk</code>; the four-part zero-baseline cleanup and foreign-resource non-mutation are inherited from <code class=\"notranslate\">createCleanupGates()</code> (post-<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5308231548\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1855\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1855/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1855\">#1855</a> ownership proof).</li>\n<li>Evidence for closure: one <code class=\"notranslate\">e2e-cli-prod</code> run at a canary tag with the <code class=\"notranslate\">readme.quickstart</code> transcript attached; that run is the canary-admission gate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Dependency: none hard on <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5314539607\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1880\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1880/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1880\">#1880</a> — if the README walk fails at the readiness seam, that is gate-2 evidence, per this issue's Boundaries.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Not started: requires a canary-admission slot; runtime is exercised only on the hosted prod runner (no local lease needed). Recommend <code class=\"notranslate\">status:plan</code>, milestone stays <code class=\"notranslate\">0.0.7</code> unless the coordinator retargets after Canary 7.</p>"}],"url":"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1881","title":"rickylabs/netscript Issue #1881 comments","display_url":"https://github.com/rickylabs/netscript/issues/1881","display_title":"rickylabs/netscript Issue #1881 comments"},"_meta":null},"error":null,"durationMs":509},"threadId":"01a06491-c069-7610-999b-e4f3efa4096f","turnId":"01a06491-c0b5-7811-a584-1b84e145973e","completedAtMs":1788394357407},"emittedAtMs":1788394357409}
