d so the checkout is left dirty, and any operator `--smoke-root` override is silently discarded. The sibling `quickstart.walk` suite uses `context.project.smokeRoot` for exactly this reason. Fix: seed the initial cwd from `context.project.smokeRoot` (pass it as a walker argument) and stop overriding `smokeRoot` in `defaultOptions`. The workflow can then hand a fresh temp directory to the suite.\\n\\n**2. High. The AppHost path is hard-coded instead of taken from the run context.**\\n`readme-command.ts:223` builds `<repoRoot>/my-app/aspire/apphost.mts` for `aspire describe`, while cleanup at `runtime-gates.ts:294-295` uses `context.project.appHost`/`projectRoot` derived from `smokeRoot`. Today they coincide only because of finding 1. Once smokeRoot is honoured, port capture and cleanup will point at different trees. Pass `context.project.appHost` to the walker.\\n\\n**3. Medium. Runtime-edge decision logic has no unit coverage.**\\n`substituteCommand`, `commandArguments`, `firstHttpPort`, `changeDirectory`, `readState` validation, and the out-of-order guard (`readme-command.ts:54-59, 161-248, 250-282`) are unexported and untested. These encode the only two permitted substitutions, the unsupported-placeholder rejection, and the fail-at-curl-line behaviour, which are the core contract. Move the pure parts (substitution, argv split, port selection, state validation) into `src/domain/readme-quickstart.ts` beside the parser and test them. That also matches the doctrine split of pure parsing versus IO at the gate edge.\\n\\n**4. Medium. Port selection can guess.**\\n`readme-command.ts:244` falls back to 80/443 when a described URL carries no explicit port. The plan's risk register says never guess a port. Fail closed with the README curl line instead of defaulting.\\n\\n**5. Medium. README line 14 will hit the Deno 2.9 dependency-recency guard for a freshly published canary.**\\nThe sibling suite passes `--minimum-dependency-age=0` on install and on every `deno run` (`quickstart-walk-suite.ts:75,102`). The README command is executed verbatim, so a hosted run within the recency window fails at the install line. This is inherent to the fidelity contract, not a code bug, but it must be recorded in `drift.md`/worklog and the hosted canary scheduled outside the window or the README updated. Same class of risk for `aspire restore`/`start` without `--non-interactive` on a non-TTY runner; hosted evidence must prove it.\\n\\n**6. Low. Receipt fields overstate substitutions.**\\nEvery receipt records `substitutions.version` even for commands with no `<version>`, and the `aspire wait` receipt reports `port` although that command substituted nothing (`readme-command.ts:90-96`). Record only substitutions actually applied, and put the captured port under a separate evidence key.\\n\\n**7. Low. Stale receipts survive a rerun.**\\nIndex 0 resets `state.json` but leaves `receipts/05..11.json` from a prior run (`readme-command.ts:291-303`). On a clean runner this is moot, but locally it can misattribute evidence. Clear the receipts directory at index 0.\\n\\n**8. Low. No compile-time guard that ids, phases, and commands stay the same length.**\\n`readme-quickstart-suite.ts:17-43` indexes three parallel `as const` tuples by number. A future README edit that adds a command compiles but produces an `undefined` gate id at runtime. Add a `satisfies` tuple-length assertion or a unit test comparing the three lengths.\\n\\n**9. Low. Artifacts.**\\nThe worklog gate table still reports the S0 counts (223 files, 302 tests); the S1/S2 state the prompt cites (229 files, 310 tests) is not recorded there, and the drift log does not yet mention the recency-guard or non-interactive risks from finding 5.\\n\\nNot a finding: `runAspireCommand` reuse for `aspire start` is sound given the 13.5.3 help text, the parser fails closed on markers and unclosed fences, `cd` handling preserves logical cwd correctly (`cd ..` resolves to `my-app`), and `EXPENSIVE_RUNTIME_SUITE_IDS` includes the new suite.\",\"ttft_ms\":3427,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":171226,\"uuid\":\"b76307dd-85e8-474d-97a6-10061f374a71\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":2652,\"time_to_request_ms\":355,\"queued_turn_count\":0}\n","exitCode":0,"durationMs":173803},"threadId":"01a06491-c069-7610-999b-e4f3efa4096f","turnId":"01a06491-c0b5-7811-a584-1b84e145973e","completedAtMs":1788395134233},"emittedAtMs":1788395134274}
