gainst the current tree, not the summary. Static evidence: the two touched entrypoints type-check, and the domain, drift, suite, and registry tests pass (32 tests). Runtime proof stays with the hosted canary per the coordinator boundary; the lint-wrapper refusal is treated as baseline.\\n\\nEvery prior finding is resolved in code:\\n\\n- **Clean-runner cwd.** The walker seeds its logical cwd from `context.project.smokeRoot` (`readme-quickstart-suite.ts:111`, `readme-command.ts:148-155`) and the suite no longer pins `smokeRoot` to the checkout (`readme-quickstart-suite.ts:54,63`). Operator overrides are honoured.\\n- **AppHost from context.** `context.project.appHost` is passed through and used for `aspire describe` (`readme-quickstart-suite.ts:112`, `readme-command.ts:217-223`), so port capture and cleanup agree by construction.\\n- **Pure rules with tests.** Substitution, argv, and explicit-port selection live in `src/domain/readme-quickstart.ts:69-107` and are covered by `tests/domain/readme-quickstart_test.ts` including the unsupported-placeholder, quoting, and no-port-receipt failures.\\n- **No implicit port.** `explicitServicePort` skips URLs without an explicit port and fails closed (`readme-quickstart.ts:102-106`).\\n- **Receipt truthfulness.** Only substitutions actually applied are recorded; the captured port sits under `evidence` on the `aspire wait` receipt only (`readme-command.ts:104-118`).\\n- **Stale receipts** are removed at index 0 (`readme-command.ts:150-154`); no-retry, cleanup unchanged, and command fidelity all still hold.\\n- **Drift** now records the recency-guard/non-TTY admission and the missing RTK proxy.\\n\\nRemaining findings, none blocking:\\n\\n1. **Low. Wait-receipt drops the port-capture failure detail.** When `aspire describe` fails, `servicePortError` is stored in state (`readme-command.ts:229-234`) but neither the passing wait receipt nor the later curl-line error surfaces it: `substituteReadmeQuickstartCommand` reports only \\\"no port receipt exists\\\" (`readme-quickstart.ts:77`). Add the stored detail to the curl-line error or an `evidence.error` field on the wait receipt so the hosted failure trail explains why the port was missing.\\n2. **Low. Tuple alignment test is partial.** `readme-quickstart-suite_test.ts` asserts eleven command gates, which covers ids and commands, but a shorter `README_GATE_PHASES` would still pass with an undefined phase. Assert the three tuple lengths directly.\\n3. **Low. Default smoke root is still inside the checkout.** The fallback `.llm/tmp/cli-e2e` matches the sibling suite and is gitignored, so this is convention rather than a defect. The S3 workflow should pass an external `--smoke-root` if a truly out-of-tree scaffold is wanted on the hosted runner.\\n4. **Low. Worklog gate table is stale.** It still reports S0 counts (223 files, 302 tests) while the S1/S2 static gates have since run at higher counts. Refresh before the sign-off commit.\",\"ttft_ms\":4723,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":42273,\"uuid\":\"a7395046-7fb3-4e16-bdd7-c866c6b58189\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":3325,\"time_to_request_ms\":359,\"queued_turn_count\":0}\n"},"emittedAtMs":1788395344284}
