{"method":"item/commandExecution/outputDelta","params":{"threadId":"01a06491-c069-7610-999b-e4f3efa4096f","turnId":"01a06491-c0b5-7811-a584-1b84e145973e","itemId":"exec-64d17c99-7849-4e6f-92ff-97e626e0ca87","delta":"{\"duration_api_ms\":77813,\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"33acaeee-4ed1-4cca-a6c6-8fb1dd382c4c\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.71217075,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2237,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":62190,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":697515,\"output_tokens\":5405,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":2036},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":62190,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":56,\"output_tokens\":1673,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":140594,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2950,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2950},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1267,\"outputTokens\":21,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001372,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000,\"thinkingTokens\":0,\"canonicalModel\":\"claude-haiku-4-5\",\"provider\":\"firstParty\",\"costBasis\":\"list\"},\"claude-fable-5-1\":{\"inputTokens\":2237,\"outputTokens\":5405,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":697515,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":62190,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.7107987500000001,\"contextWindow\":1000000,\"maxOutputTokens\":64000,\"thinkingTokens\":2036,\"canonicalModel\":\"claude-fable-5-1\",\"provider\":\"firstParty\",\"costBasis\":\"list\"}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"fast_mode_disabled_reason\":\"sdk_opt_in_required\",\"subagent_stats\":{\"spawned\":0,\"requested\":{\"background\":0,\"foreground\":0,\"unset\":0},\"started_in_background\":0,\"max_depth\":0,\"spawned_by_subagents\":0,\"completed\":0,\"failed\":0,\"killed\":{\"parent\":0,\"user\":0,\"system\":0},\"refused\":{\"depth_limit\":0,\"concurrency_limit\":0,\"budget\":0},\"by_type\":{}},\"is_error\":false,\"num_turns\":6,\"subtype\":\"success\",\"api_error_status\":null,\"result\":\"**PASS**\\n\\nVerified against the uncommitted diff in `.github/workflows/e2e-cli-prod.yml` and the committed `readme.quickstart` suite. The YAML parses through pinned `@std/yaml` with `--no-lock`, the new step sits immediately after `quickstart.walk`, and it uses the exact report and log paths the coordinator specified. Nothing in the diff touches release refs, publication, tags, or Canary 8. Runtime suites were not run.\\n\\nWhat holds up:\\n\\n- **Step wiring** (`e2e-cli-prod.yml:137-145`): condition mirrors the walk step exactly, so the suite runs even when scaffold.runtime or walk fails but only once the published CLI and workspace installs succeeded. `--source jsr` plus `--cli jsr:@netscript/cli@<version>` satisfies the suite's fail-closed guard in `readme-quickstart-suite.ts:120-129`, and `--cleanup` engages the shared cleanup tail, which the runner executes in a `finally` block even on gate failure.\\n- **Failure reporting** (`e2e-cli-prod.yml:151`): the new report joins the loop; a readme failure fails the job, so `failure()` fires and the summary tool reads it with the same `|| true` guard as siblings.\\n- **Artifact upload** (`e2e-cli-prod.yml:174-177`): report, NDJSON log, `state.json`, and the per-command receipts match the paths written by `readme-quickstart-suite.ts:115` and `readme-command.ts:294-302`. Existing artifact entries are untouched, so no evidence is weakened.\\n- **Interaction with siblings**: the readme suite hard-codes project name `my-app` under `.llm/tmp/cli-e2e`, while scaffold.runtime and walk use timestamped names, so no directory collision on a fresh runner.\\n\\nFindings, all low severity and non-blocking:\\n\\n1. **Low** `e2e-cli-prod.yml:140-145`: the step omits `--format pretty`, unlike both sibling steps. The run command defaults to NDJSON on stdout, so the CI log for this step will be machine-formatted rather than human-readable. The report and log-file outputs are unaffected. Consider adding the flag for consistency if the coordinator is open to it.\\n2. **Low** `readme-command.ts:160-167`: `initializeState` clears prior receipts but not a pre-existing `my-app` project directory, and `netscript init my-app` runs without `--force`. Harmless in CI because each runner is fresh, but a local rerun after an aborted run would fail at command 2. Out of the S3 workflow scope; noting for the suite owner.\\n3. **Info**: gate receipts under `.llm/tmp/gate-receipts/readme.quickstart/` are not uploaded. This matches the sibling suites, which also do not upload theirs, so it is consistent rather than a regression.\",\"ttft_ms\":3273,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":78228,\"uuid\":\"c16d3b56-f94e-40ea-92dd-c99829111f4f\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":2490,\"time_to_request_ms\":302,\"queued_turn_count\":0}\n"},"emittedAtMs":1788395639269}
