ry tool reads it with the same `|| true` guard as siblings.\\n- **Artifact upload** (`e2e-cli-prod.yml:174-177`): report, NDJSON log, `state.json`, and the per-command receipts match the paths written by `readme-quickstart-suite.ts:115` and `readme-command.ts:294-302`. Existing artifact entries are untouched, so no evidence is weakened.\\n- **Interaction with siblings**: the readme suite hard-codes project name `my-app` under `.llm/tmp/cli-e2e`, while scaffold.runtime and walk use timestamped names, so no directory collision on a fresh runner.\\n\\nFindings, all low severity and non-blocking:\\n\\n1. **Low** `e2e-cli-prod.yml:140-145`: the step omits `--format pretty`, unlike both sibling steps. The run command defaults to NDJSON on stdout, so the CI log for this step will be machine-formatted rather than human-readable. The report and log-file outputs are unaffected. Consider adding the flag for consistency if the coordinator is open to it.\\n2. **Low** `readme-command.ts:160-167`: `initializeState` clears prior receipts but not a pre-existing `my-app` project directory, and `netscript init my-app` runs without `--force`. Harmless in CI because each runner is fresh, but a local rerun after an aborted run would fail at command 2. Out of the S3 workflow scope; noting for the suite owner.\\n3. **Info**: gate receipts under `.llm/tmp/gate-receipts/readme.quickstart/` are not uploaded. This matches the sibling suites, which also do not upload theirs, so it is consistent rather than a regression.\",\"ttft_ms\":3273,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":78228,\"uuid\":\"c16d3b56-f94e-40ea-92dd-c99829111f4f\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":2490,\"time_to_request_ms\":302,\"queued_turn_count\":0}\n","exitCode":0,"durationMs":81068},"threadId":"01a06491-c069-7610-999b-e4f3efa4096f","turnId":"01a06491-c0b5-7811-a584-1b84e145973e","completedAtMs":1788395639544},"emittedAtMs":1788395639572}
